=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# Note$
# Compare mode: each section shows the current pattern, as$
# hardn's components render it today (P-23, P-24; built), and$
# beside it or under it the proposed one (P-42): a mock after$
# Figma's rows, drawn by the gallery. No component changed.$
# Proposed: the subject at column 6 and its state, a coloured$
# word with no colon, in one column after it; notices as$
# callouts, neutral lines as muted prose.$
# Markers: Figma's status markers for a step done, failed or$
# rolled back, as here, in place of the key-value bullet, which$
# -marker bullet shows.$
# Status column: two cells after the widest title, as here; with$
# -column figma it is Figma's column 27, which these titles$
# reach, so their rows stack at every width.$
$
# compare countdown --------------------------------------------$
$
# Current ------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Warning: This change reverts automatically in 2:45$
      To keep it, open a new SSH session and run:$
      sudo hardn confirm$
$
  [ ] Warning: This change reverts automatically in 2:45$
      To keep it, open a new SSH session on port 2230 and run:$
      sudo hardn confirm$
$
  [!] Urgent: This change reverts automatically in 0:05$
      To keep it, open a new SSH session and run:$
      sudo hardn confirm$
$
# Proposed -----------------------------------------------------$
$
# Warning$
# This change reverts automatically in 2:45$
# To keep it, open a new SSH session and run:$
$
      $ sudo hardn confirm$
$
# Warning$
# This change reverts automatically in 2:45$
# To keep it, open a new SSH session on port 2230 and run:$
$
      $ sudo hardn confirm$
$
# Urgent$
# This change reverts automatically in 0:05$
# To keep it, open a new SSH session and run:$
$
      $ sudo hardn confirm$
$
$

